=== Fix round, 2026-08-15 ===
Host: macOS (Darwin 25.5.0). No ngspice run required for this benchmark by
design (design.md sec. 9): the gate is the hand-computed T10 budget plus
assertions A1-A10.

Review findings addressed:
1. MUST-FIX: the claim "dropout 500 mV max at 1 A" for the AP7361C was not a
   datasheet figure. Verified against Diodes AP7361C datasheet DS37274
   Rev. 5-2 (Oct 2020), downloaded from
   https://www.diodes.com/assets/Datasheets/AP7361C.pdf and text-extracted:
   - EC table, VDROPOUT, IOUT = 1 A, 2.6V<=VOUT<=3.3V row: 340 mV TYP,
     max column is "-" (no max specified). Features page quotes
     "360mV at 1A Typical" for 3.3 V.
   - Restated in design.md sec. 4, power-tree.yaml (U2_ldo.dropout_v) and
     assertions.yaml A4 as: 340 mV typ (datasheet); 0.50 V/A explicitly
     labeled a conservative in-house guardband assumption, not vendor data.
   - A4 recomputed under both bases at i_load = 0.3917 A,
     v_ldo_in = 3.819 V, vout_max = 3.366 V:
       datasheet typ:      vdo = 0.34 x 0.3917 = 0.133 V -> margin +0.320 V
       in-house guardband: vdo = 0.50 x 0.3917 = 0.196 V -> margin +0.257 V
     A4 PASS under both rows.
2. Advisory: A5 now cites the datasheet SOT-223 theta_JA: same DS37274
   Rev. 5-2 thermal table, SOT223 = 110 C/W (FR-4, minimum recommended pad
   layout, still air; table note 9). Added row at 110 C/W:
     P_worst = (4.902-3.234) x 0.3917 + 4.902 x 60e-6 = 0.654 W
     Tj = 50 + 0.654 x 110 = 121.9 C  -> +3.1 C to the 125 C design gate.
   121.9 C < 125 C at every stated condition, so A5 remains PASS, but is now
   marked "PASS (layout-dependent)": the +34.5 C margin requires the assumed
   62 C/W (~1 in^2 pour, AN1028); at datasheet minimum-pad theta_JA the
   headroom is only 3.1 C. Datasheet operating Tj range is -40..150 C and
   thermal shutdown ~150 C; 125 C is the design's own gate.
3. Advisory: power-tree.yaml usb_host now documents the 500 mA budget
   assumption: Type-C default-power source (>= 500 mA without enumeration at
   default Rp); the USB 2.0 100 mA pre-enumeration/legacy-host allocation is
   declared out of scope, with rationale (no PD/BC1.2 sensing, no throttling
   path; Wi-Fi TX peak ~395 mA cannot fit 100 mA; firmware note for strictly
   compliant legacy hosts).

Arithmetic re-check (python3 script, run 2026-08-15): 17/17 checks PASS --
load sums (wifi_tx_peak typ/worst), A2 VBUS sum 0.39491 A and +105.1 mA
margin, voltage propagation worst_min 3.819 V (computed 3.8184, rounding
noted), A4 both dropout rows, A5 P/Tj at 62 and 110 C/W (typ and worst),
A6 +205 mA. No assertion window was widened; no status changed except
A5 PASS -> PASS (layout-dependent), which narrows rather than weakens the
claim.

Remaining stated assumptions (unchanged, still flagged in-file): SS34 Vf at
0.4 A, PTC initial-resistance range, 62 C/W pour-dependent theta_JA target.

=== Fix round 2 (re-review response), 2026-08-15 ===
Nothing above is retracted or rewritten; the round-1 numbers that this round
corrects are left in place so the history reads honestly. Where round 1 and
this section disagree, THIS section supersedes.

Primary-source verification (not taken from round 1's notes):
- Datasheet re-checked directly from the local PDF, Diodes AP7361C
  DS37274 Rev. 5 - 2, October 2020, sha256
  9b64f49c5975b2baf2360248a75212599bde8bf083d315d936e4f1c93b2e1f92.
  * VDROPOUT, IOUT = 1 A, 2.6V<=VOUT<=3.3V: min "-", TYP 340, max "-" (mV).
    No max column value exists. Features page: "Very Low Dropout Voltage
    (3.3V): 360mV at 1A Typical". CONFIRMS round 1; the original
    "500 mV max at 1 A" remains a fabrication and is gone from the files.
  * theta_JA, SOT223 (Note 9): 110 C/W typ. CONFIRMS round 1's value.
  * TJ operating range -40 to +150 C; TSHDN 150 C typ, hysteresis 20 C;
    PD(SOT223) 1100 mW. All as cited.
- ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 datasheet spot-check: 355 mA @ 802.11b 1 Mbps 20.5 dBm
  and 8 uA deep-sleep (RTC mem + RTC periph powered) both confirmed.

Corrections made THIS round (all found by re-running the arithmetic, all
were errors in the optimistic direction or unsupported attributions):
1. theta_JA attribution overstated. Note 9 for SOT-223 reads only "mounted
   on FR-4 substrate PC board, with minimum recommended pad layout" -- it
   states NO airflow condition and NO board size. Round 1 called it "still
   air" (the review advisory's wording); that phrase is not in the
   datasheet. Removed from design.md and assertions.yaml A5.
2. V_ldo_in worst_min was written 3.819 V; exact value is 3.81834 V, which
   rounds to 3.818 V. Round 1 logged this as "rounding noted" and kept the
   favorable digit. Corrected to 3.818 V in power-tree.yaml and A4.
3. A4 datasheet-typ margin followed from (2): +0.320 V -> +0.319 V
   (exact 0.31920). The guardband row is unchanged at +0.257 V
   (exact 0.25654). A4 still PASSes under both bases.
4. A4 used i_load = 0.3917 A; the actual LDO OUTPUT current at
   wifi_tx_peak worst is 0.3916 A (0.391601; the 60 uA Iq flows Vin->GND
   and is not output current). Corrected, and i_load_a is now an explicit
   input field rather than an unexplained constant.
5. V_ldo_in max was written 4.902 V (truncated); exact 4.90261 -> 4.903 V.
   Corrected in power-tree.yaml and A5. P and Tj are unchanged to the
   quoted precision (0.654 W; 90.5 C at 62 C/W; 121.9 C at 110 C/W).
6. A4 secondary row usbc_min_4p75_guardband: 4.335 - 3.562 = 0.77355,
   which rounds to +0.774 V, not +0.773 V. Corrected, and the row is now
   labelled as mixing usbc-min input voltage with worst-current required
   V_in (conservative, not self-consistent).
7. A5 caveat now states the breach condition explicitly: at the 110 C/W
   minimum-pad figure, Ta > 53.1 C exceeds the 125 C gate
   (Ta_max = 125 - 0.654 x 110 = 53.09 C); at 62 C/W, Ta_max = 84.5 C.
   NOTE: 53.1 C was itself wrong in my first draft of this edit (52.8 C)
   and was corrected after computing it. A5 stays PASS (layout-dependent):
   121.9 C < 125 C at every stated condition.

